        <div class="sup-demo-copy"><p class="sup-lede sup-body-p">There is no motor. The wheels turn the brushes, and they turn them fast: one turn of the wheels spins the brushes five times. So you walk at a normal pace and the brushes are moving quick enough to flick the leaves up off the grass and into the hopper behind you. Nothing gets pushed into a pile, because there is no pile.</p><p class="sup-lede sup-body-p">Three 300 liter yard bags come free with every Sweep, so the bagging is handled before you start. Tip a full hopper into one and the bag still is not full.</p></div>
