        <p class="sup-eyebrow">The cost of the bend</p>
        <h2 class="sup-h2">Nobody minds the raking. It is the forty times you bend down after it.</h2>
        <p class="sup-lede sup-body-p">You blow the leaves into a pile. Then you rake what the blower missed. Then you bend down, forty or fifty times, scooping armfuls into a bag that will not stay open. Then you do it again next Saturday because more came down overnight.</p>
        <p class="sup-lede sup-body-p">Four separate motions to move leaves about twenty feet. If your back hurts from bending and raking leaves, that is the part this removes. Not the walking. The bending.</p>
        <p class="sup-note">It weighs 29.77 lb and you supply the power. There is no motor. If pushing a mower is already too much, this will be too.</p>
